    "submit a project",
    "// How to join us",
    "Send us your project details and share what you aim to achieve with the community.",
    "Create your collective page and make it visible to supporters and contributors.",
    "Begin accepting donations and manage your finances transparently with ease.",
    "submit a project",
    "// become a funder",
    "OSE offers a trusted, compliant channel for donations and grants in both the EU and the US. Thanks to ED certification, US foundations can give tax-deductible grants.",
    "contact us",
    "// conditions",
    "We want to make sure every project aligns with our collective values. To join, developers need to meet a few conditions:",
    "The project is open and transparent in fund management",
    "The team is ready to communicate clearly with the community",
    "There is a commitment to use funds responsibly",
    "These conditions help maintain trust and quality within the community.",
    "// pricing",
    "OSE charges an 8% fee on incoming funds, plus payment provider fees & 10% on public grants and subsidies.. No setup fees. No hidden costs.",
    "// faq",
    "Do I need to create a legal entity?",
    "No. OSE provides the fiscal structure so you don’t have to.",
    "Do you control my project?",
    "No. Your project remains fully autonomous: your project, your rules.",
    "How long does it take to get started?",
    "Most projects are live within a week.",
    "Who can apply?",
    "Any open source project, regardless of size or maturity.",
    "Do we lose independence?",
    "No. Your project remains fully yours: your project, your rules.",
